#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:2
msgid "Global tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:4
msgid ""
"This guide covers how to use poethepoet as a global task runner, for private "
"user level tasks instead of shared project level tasks. Global tasks are "
"available anywhere, and serve a similar purpose to shell aliases or scripts "
"on the ``PATH`` — but as poe tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:6
msgid "There are two steps required to make this work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:8
msgid ""
"Create a project somewhere central such as ``~/.poethepoet`` where you "
"define tasks that you want to have globally accessible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:9
msgid ""
"Configure an alias in your shell's startup script such as ``alias "
"edgar=\"poe -C ~/.poethepoet\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:13
msgid ""
"This document suggests calling your alias `edgar` — because it's a pun... "
"but you can use any alternative name you fancy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:15
msgid ""
"The project at ``~/.poethepoet`` can be a regular poetry project including "
"dependencies or just a file with tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:17
msgid ""
"You can choose any location to define the tasks, and whatever name you like "
"for the global poe alias."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:21
msgid ""
"For this to work Poe the Poet must be installed globally such as via pipx or "
"homebrew."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:25
msgid "Shell completions for global tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:27
msgid ""
"If you use zsh or fish then the usual completion script should just work "
"with your alias (as long as it was created with poethepoet >=0.28.0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:29
msgid ""
"However for bash you'll need to generate a new completion script for the "
"alias specifying the alias and the path to you global tasks like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:31
msgid ""
"# System bash\n"
"poe _bash_completion edgar ~/.poethepoet > /etc/bash_completion.d/edgar.bash-"
"completion\n"
"\n"
"# Homebrew bash\n"
"poe _bash_completion edgar ~/.poethepoet > $(brew --prefix)/etc/"
"bash_completion.d/edgar.bash-completion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:41
msgid ""
"These examples assume your global poe alias is ``edgar``, and your global "
"tasks live at ``~/.poethepoet``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/global_tasks.rst:43
msgid ""
"How to ensure installed bash completions are enabled may vary depending on "
"your system."
msgstr ""
